  "summary": "Full assessment of all 566 French/Vietnamese passages: seventeen chapter headings and every paragraph of the novella, translated directly from the French. The first reviews scored 8.55, 8.35 and 8.80 across three ranges and found four majors (a rhetorical question turned upside down, ‘vợ trước’ for children, a brother-in-law kinship slip, and a literally rendered idiom of ruin); one round of fixes and fresh separate-context blind reviews of the two failing ranges then scored 8.85 (units 1–181) and 8.85 (182–369), with the third range already passing at 8.80, and no major or critical finding open. A reversed sense at unit 153 that the review had missed was also corrected in the fix round. The final score is taken from the weakest range, 8.80 on the half-point scale, above the unchanged 8.6 threshold. A few minor points remain open.",
